## Import

An existing user configuration can be imported with its path (or `file://<path>`)
as ID. It is read with docker-agent's own types, and `pulumi import` generates the typed inputs,
`path` included. The file is adopted: the import writes nothing and takes no backup, `overwrite` is
not needed, and deleting the resource leaves the file in place (with the content Pulumi last wrote) instead of
removing it. The resource ID is the file's absolute path.

```sh
$ pulumi import docker-agent:index:UserSettings settings ~/.config/cagent/config.yaml
```

docker-agent:index:getAgent.description:
Reads a Docker Agent configuration from an OCI registry, like `docker agent share pull`,
without writing anything to disk.

The reference can be a tag or a digest. When the provider's `registryAuth` has credentials for the registry,
they are used right away. Otherwise the function first tries anonymous access and retries with the Docker
credential store when the registry answers 401, 403, 404 or 429. It accepts artifacts pushed by
`docker agent share push` and by `AgentArtifact`, and
rejects manifests without the `io.docker.agent.version` annotation.

{{% examples %}}
